# ============================================================
# FLUOROSAM + CONVLSTM GUIDEWIRE TRACKING — GUIDE3D POC
# ============================================================
# Author: Tim Chen
# Description:
# -----------
# Proof-of-concept pipeline for automatic guidewire segmentation
# and temporal tracking in fluoroscopy video.
#
# The model combines:
#
# 1. A pretrained FluoroSAM image encoder for spatial feature
# extraction from individual fluoroscopy frames.
#
# 2. A ConvLSTM temporal module that processes consecutive
# frame features to model guidewire movement over time.
#
# 3. A lightweight segmentation decoder that produces a
# binary guidewire probability mask.
#
# Post-processing is used to:
#
# - retain the largest predicted guidewire component
# - skeletonize the segmentation
# - identify candidate endpoints
# - estimate and temporally smooth the guidewire tip
# - visualize the guidewire, tip position, and recent trajectory
#
# Dataset
# -------
# Uses the official Guide3D dataset.
#
# Guide3D contains fluoroscopy recordings acquired from guidewires
# manipulated inside a vascular phantom. It does not contain
# real-patient fluoroscopy procedures.
#
# Demo Output
# -----------
# The inference-only mode can load an existing trained checkpoint
# and export:
#
# - original phantom fluoroscopy video
# - AI guidewire tracking overlay
# - side-by-side comparison video
# - combined comparison montage
# - JSON output manifest
#
# Intended Use
# ------------
# Research and technical demonstration only.
# This implementation is a proof of concept and has not been
# clinically validated. It must not be used for diagnosis,
# treatment, procedural navigation, or clinical decision-making.
# ============================================================

